course: dictionary
lesson: 7586
title: Looking back with previously
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Previously means before, at an earlier time. It is a word for looking back. When a TV show starts with «Previously on…», it is reminding you what happened before.
explain: Previously can also mean before the time being talked about. In a maths lesson, «the number previously found» is the answer you got earlier. In everyday speech you would say before or earlier, so swap one of those in to check your meaning.
explain: Previously owned means someone else had it first, so it is second-hand. A previously owned bike had an earlier owner. Look for clues in the sentence, such as «before» or a word about the past.
fact: Previously means before, at an earlier time.
fact: «Previously on…» at the start of a show reminds you what happened before.
fact: Previously owned means second-hand, owned by someone earlier.
fact: «As previously mentioned» means «I already told you this»; it is office jargon.
fact: To check the meaning, swap in before or earlier and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Previously on…» at the start of the show reminds us what happened before. What does previously mean here? | After the end of the show | Live, right now | *Before, at an earlier time | Very loudly
exercise: «The bike was previously owned, so it was cheaper.» What does previously owned mean? | Stolen | Painted red | Brand new from the shop | *Owned by someone earlier, second-hand
exercise: Mum says, «As previously mentioned, the meeting is at four.» What does she mean? | The meeting has been cancelled | I have a surprise for you | *I already told you this | I want more tea
test:
Maths: «The number previously found was 12.» What does previously mean in this sentence? | Later | *Earlier | Never | Quietly
Which word means the same as previously? | Tomorrow | Louder | *Before | Nearby
exam: Which sentence uses previously correctly to mean before? | The castle will previously be visited tomorrow. | Previously, she visits the castle every day next week. | The castle was previously a bright red colour, but it is now the same. | *She had previously visited the castle, so she knew the way.
